s","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"009bb879161ef2af6f6c0ffed58dfc12d065eab087434a3c1e0591ac863c3df2"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":426800,"output_tokens":6935,"requests":15}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"b51473c9416742c36bd8189b8ba4496247fe2b8c62c851c04f1f8310f701d2c6"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:project.symbol-reference-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":309286,"output_tokens":5571,"requests":13}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Require the synthetic-advisory-key test (AC-7/AC-8) to use a non-string, list-shaped value (mirroring similar_tickets) so it actually exercises the generic pass-through for the advisory shape this story introduces.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3875,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC-7: 'adding a synthetic advisory key at the create_core boundary and asserting it reaches the create return dict' — type unspecified","A list-shaped value is nulled by log_advisory_warning (gates.py:308) while a string passes"],"finding":"Acceptance criteria 7 and 8 (synthetic-advisory-key reaches create and idea return dicts) do not fix the TYPE of the synthetic key. A string-typed synthetic key would pass even if the generic path coerces values through the string-only transform, so the test would NOT catch similar_tickets (a list) being dropped — the exact failure mode the genericity work exists to prevent.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f612a8b6a83439c0c","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria lines 7–8 ('Advisory keys propagate from create_core ... without a per-key edit' / 'The same synthetic advisory key reaches the idea() return dict')","norm_id":"nda6d04189d10b31b","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer makes the synthetic key a string; test passes; similar_tickets (list) is still silently nulled in the library/idea return dicts"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Amend AC-7/AC-8 to inject a list-valued synthetic advisory key and assert the list arrives structurally intact (not coerced to null).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"State that the generic return-dict pass-through must carry the list-valued `similar_tickets` through unchanged (not via the string-only `log_advisory_warning`/`_warn_advisory` transform, which nulls non-strings), and specify whether/how the list is logged on the library channel.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3906,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the return-dict pass-through is made generic at the create_core boundary'","gates.py:308 `text = warning if isinstance(warning, str) and warning else None` — a list returns None","similar_tickets is 'a similar_tickets array' / 'ranked list' per the plan, not a string","_lib_writes.py:172,224 route duplicate_warning through _warn_advisory (=log_advisory_warning)"],"finding":"The 'generic return-dict pass-through' may silently drop the list-valued similar_tickets if it reuses the existing string-only advisory transform. In _lib_writes.py the current advisory keys are passed through log_advisory_warning (gates.py:302-311), which does `isinstance(warning, str)` and returns None for any non-string; similar_tickets is a list of dicts, so a generic path that funnels all advisory keys through that transform would null it. The plan scopes genericity to the return dict but never states the list-valued advisory must bypass the string-logging transform.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f9ceb7dd2b4dbff18","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'The advisory seam' and 'What \"generic\" does and does not cover'; _lib_writes.py:171-180,223-232; gates.py:302-311","norm_id":"n04f0344642901076","priority":0.4094,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Generic pass-through reuses log_advisory_warning for every advisory key → similar_tickets becomes None in the library create_ticket and idea return dicts even though retrieval returned ranked results"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify the generic mechanism as a structural copy of advisory keys from create_core's result into the return dict that does NOT coerce values through the string-advisory logger, and note that similar_tickets (list) is passed through verbatim.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.6111,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_