_ticket output carries similar_tickets. Checked by: an MCP test asserting the key is present in the tool result.'","The MCP create_ticket ToolSpec at src/rebar/_mcp_tool_specs.py:306-320 uses post=(with_push,) and library='create_ticket', so it passes the full library create_ticket return dict through rather than hand-picking keys (contrast id_alias_only at _mcp_derive.py:254-255, wired only to log_session at :465) — the library-level genericity the plan describes is what carries the key to MCP, but the plan never states this.","A prior plan-review cache entry raised this same gap."],"finding":"The plan asserts an MCP create_ticket acceptance criterion but never enumerates the MCP tool as a consumer path in the Approach, nor traces how the advisory reaches it; MCP is not among the five create_core callers the scope table lists.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f922ec1bdcbda5615","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / 'the five callers it actually has' table and AC 'MCP create_ticket output carries similar_tickets'","norm_id":"n389c08750239e537","priority":0.0978,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reader verifying scope cannot confirm the MCP AC is satisfiable without independently discovering that create_ticket's ToolSpec passes the library dict through unmodified.","If a future refactor added an id_alias_only-style projection to create_ticket, the MCP AC would silently break with no plan text flagging the dependency."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a row/sentence to the caller discussion noting the MCP create_ticket tool routes through library create_ticket (post=(with_push,) in _mcp_tool_specs.py, which does not strip keys), so the same return-dict genericity that covers the library result also covers MCP output.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed